Package: OptCutR
Type: Package
Title: Optimal Cut-point Discovery and Validation
Version: 0.1.0
Author: Payton Yau [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Payton Yau <tungon@gmail.com>
Description: 
    Provides a comprehensive workflow to determine, find, and 
    validate optimal cut-points for continuous predictors. It handles 
    both survival (time-to-event) and binary classification outcomes. 
    The package includes functions to first determine the optimal number 
    of cut-points, then find their locations using either a systematic 
    search or a genetic algorithm (for multiple cut-points), and finally 
    to assess the stability of the result via bootstrapping.
